title: Auto-seal hook (A) + multi-writer admission Phase C v1 (C) — the collision-ending protocol, proven
summary: |-
  Built 'A then C'. A: a post-commit auto-seal hook so the fabric grows automatically on every git commit — it immediately proved itself by recording BOTH agents' commits (mine + the concurrent classroom agent's) into one attributed history. C: the multi-writer admission protocol (Phase C v1) — SCRATCH fork + admitDecision (FAST_ADMIT/CLEAN/KNOT/DANGLE) with the gate-rule confidence — proven by a test where two agents edit the same line, git merge-tree CONFLICTS, but Warpline admits CLEAN. A profound corollary emerged: dependency-linked concurrent edits almost always KNOT (caught by Merkle propagation), so CLEAN admissions are almost always between INDEPENDENT symbols (carrying the false-AUTOFOLD blind-spot) — which is exactly why CLEAN confidence defaults to 'independent'.</summary>
