body: |-
  A — AUTO-SEAL (#hook): install/uninstall/status manage a BEGIN/END-guarded block APPENDED to the repo's post-commit hook (coexists with Paradigm's history capture, idempotent, clean uninstall, worktree-correct path via gitPath). Seals `--ref HEAD` (the committed tree, never the worktree — clean attribution, no conflation of other agents' uncommitted work), in the BACKGROUND (full-repo absorb is slow) and fail-safe (`|| true`). `#pick` gained commit-derived intent/actor (so the hook seals with no -m) + `--quiet`. PROVEN LIVE: the hook sealed the classroom agent's commit (seq 2) and the #hook commit (seq 3) into the shared fabric automatically. A .warpline-only commit changes no meaning, so its own auto-seal no-ops — the ledger settles instead of trailing forever.

  C — MULTI-WRITER ADMISSION (#scratch, #admit, Phase C v1): forkScratch pins a per-agent optimistic base (O(1), zero contention — git's single shared working-tree/index/HEAD cannot). admitDecision(base, proposed, selvage) is the pure verdict: NOOP / FAST_ADMIT (selvage unadvanced) / CLEAN (predict autoClean — concurrent edits commute in MEANING where git conflicts on bytes) / KNOT (same symbol contradictory — human DECIDE, never silently merged) / DANGLE. CLEAN carries the GATE-RULE confidence: 'linked' (changed sets dependency-adjacent in-graph → trustworthy) vs 'independent' (disjoint → autoClean may hide a cross-symbol semantic conflict, per T-013).

  THE PROOF (test/multiwriter-admit.test.ts): foo and bar on ONE physical line; A edits foo, B edits bar → git merge-tree CONFLICTS (both rewrote the line), but admitDecision(base, B, selvage=A) → CLEAN, confidence=independent. KNOT control (both edit foo) → KNOT. LINKED control (A adds caller→bar, B edits bar) → CLEAN, confidence=linked. 146 tests green.

  THE COROLLARY (important): under body edits, ANY dependency linkage between two writers' changes routes a shared symbol's essence to both sides via Merkle-by-target → KNOT. So dependency-linked concurrent edits almost always get CAUGHT, and CLEAN admissions are almost always between INDEPENDENT symbols — which is precisely the false-AUTOFOLD blind spot. This validates defaulting CLEAN confidence to 'independent' and surfacing it as a watch flag.

  v1 SCOPE / v2 GAP: v1 is the admission DECISION + the FAST_ADMIT seal. Producing the MERGED bytes for a CLEAN re-base (so the agent's tree reflects base+other+agent) is the meaning→bytes materialization layer (GAP-7 / write-path), deferred to v2. That's the last gap between 'Warpline decides the merge' and 'Warpline performs the merge'.

  Commits: 1064c41b (#hook), e9c37b93 (ledger catch-up), 326c9ac5 (#admit/#scratch). All pushed to origin/warpline-surfaces.</parameter>
